(Rationale) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 20 Tf
23. TL
0. g
39.6850393700787407 705.8270078740157487 Td
(In busy modern airports, manually tracking flight schedules,) Tj
T* (assigning runways, and managing emergency arrivals leads to) Tj
T* (operational delays, increased human error, and heightened safety) Tj
T* (risks. Conventional procedural approaches often lack the) Tj
T* (modularity required to handle complex real-time decision-making,) Tj
T* (such as priority queues for low-fuel aircraft.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (The Airport Runway & Flight Manager system addresses these) Tj
T* (issues by centralizing flight monitoring and runway allocation) Tj
T* (into a single C++ application. By utilizing Object-Oriented) Tj
T* (Programming \(OOP\), the project models real-world entities—such) Tj
T* (as flights, runways, and priority queues—into software objects,) Tj
T* (providing structured data management, automated emergency) Tj
T* (detection, and efficient runway scheduling.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Furthermore, air traffic controllers require immediate visibility) Tj
T* (into critical parameters like aircraft fuel levels and runway) Tj
T* (maintenance statuses. By replacing fragmented, manual logs with) Tj
T* (an integrated computational system, operators can automatically) Tj
T* (re-evaluate queues whenever an incoming flight experiences low) Tj
T* (fuel reserves, ensuring rapid response times during high-stress) Tj
T* (scenarios.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Ultimately, this software provides a robust foundation for scalable) Tj
T* (airport resource management. Implementing data structures and) Tj
T* (class-based abstractions allows new capabilities, such as) Tj
T* (multi-terminal support or advanced conflict detection, to be) Tj
T* (seamlessly integrated into the software architecture without) Tj
T* (disrupting existing core operational logic.) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 14 Tf
