0. g
39.6850393700787407 705.8270078740157487 Td
(Object-Oriented Programming \(OOP\) is a paradigm centered) Tj
T* (around objects containing data fields and associated methods.) Tj
T* (Key OOP concepts applied in this system include Encapsulation,) Tj
T* (abstraction, inheritance, polymorphism, and file handling.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Classes serve as blueprints for objects such as flights and) Tj
T* (runways, bundling attributes and behavioral functions together.) Tj
T* (Inheritance enables class hierarchies to share common) Tj
T* (characteristics, while polymorphism allows functions like) Tj
T* (priority calculation or display formatting to behave dynamically) Tj
T* (based on object types. File stream handling \(fstream\) ensures) Tj
T* (data persistence across sessions by reading and writing records to) Tj
T* (binary dat files.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Encapsulation safeguards internal variables—such as flight IDs,) Tj
T* (aircraft types, and runway occupancy statuses—by restricting) Tj
T* (direct modification and providing access exclusively through) Tj
T* (defined member functions. Constructive use of destructors and) Tj
T* (constructors facilitates proper memory management during) Tj
T* (object instantiation and cleanup.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Additionally, runtime polymorphism via virtual functions allows) Tj
T* (the system to process general flight and runway entities through) Tj
T* (uniform interface calls, adapting dynamically depending on) Tj
T* (specific subtypes. The C++ Standard Template Library \(STL\)) Tj
T* (stream utilities streamline formatted input/output operations and) Tj
T* (record-keeping, forming the underlying infrastructure for reliable) Tj
T* (disk persistent storage.) Tj
ET
