(The Airport Runway & Flight Manager successfully demonstrates) Tj
T* (the application of object-oriented programming concepts to solve) Tj
T* (complex real-world scheduling problems. By encapsulating flight) Tj
T* (details, runway states, and operational statistics within C++) Tj
T* (classes, the project provides an efficient, modular solution for) Tj
T* (airport centralization.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (The implemented priority queue ensures safety by automatically) Tj
T* (prioritizing emergency landings for low-fuel aircraft. Persistent) Tj
T* (data handling via standard C++ file streams guarantees that flight) Tj
T* (logs, schedule records, and airport settings are saved across) Tj
T* (sessions. Overall, the project met all core software design) Tj
T* (objectives and reinforced concepts of object-oriented design, file) Tj
T* (processing, and menu-driven system architecture.) Tj
